data.content:
**Yes, C# fully supports `stackalloc`'d `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>`.** Both work as expected:

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[4];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system each element is 8 bytes. The only gotcha is that `sizeof(nint)` requires an `unsafe` context (use `nint.Size` instead in safe code), but `stackalloc` itself works fine in a safe context when assigned directly to a `Span<T>`.
